    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Candida or mumps skin Ag inj: moderately effective for recalcitrant warts in pts w a (+) skin Ag pretest (SORT B)"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Bleomycin 0.1% solution often cures stubborn plantar and periungual warts, though AAFP calls it unproven; Raynaud syndrome or vasc damage may follow, esp if injected @ the base of a digit"
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Interferon alfa (intralesional 3 ×/wk for 3 to 5 wks, or IM) and intralesional 5-fluorouracil (w lidocaine and Epi) have cleared recalcitrant warts"
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
